    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36501" root="كأب" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَئِيبٌ</span></b>  (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَئِبٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَكْتَئِبٌ</span></b>  (K)
A man <i>in an evil state, and broken</i> [<i>in spirit</i>] <i>by
grief,</i> or <i>mourning;</i> (S, K;) <i>in grief, unhappy,
sorrowful,</i> or <i>sad.</i> (K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَئِيبَةٌ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَأْبَآءُ</span></b>  <i>the
same,</i> as applied to a woman. (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الارض</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَئِيبَةُ الوَجْهِ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>The earth,</i> or <i>land, is of sad
aspect.</i>] (TA.)

